From: Tetris port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: mt6315: validate explicitly owned mode phases

Registering a subset of BUCK rails is not enough to establish mode ownership:
VBUCK1 FAST or FAST-to-NORMAL requests can alter several phase bits.
For boards that explicitly describe buck1-mode-mask, reject a mask reaching
outside the described available rails before registering any regulator.
Never silently truncate a coupled mask.

Preserve historical default coupled-phase behavior when the property is
absent: existing MT8192/MT8195 boards describe only selected outputs of
physically coupled bucks. Described-output presence does not prove their
historical physical phase topology incorrect. Tetris's USID-6 inventory
explicitly supplies mask 1, matching Nothing B4.1 commit
ee2be53cb75670b548948636a0db1d1ff112bf12, and remains disabled.

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/mt6315-regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/mt6315-regulator.c
--- a/drivers/regulator/mt6315-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/mt6315-regulator.c
@@ -280,6 +280,15 @@ static int mt6315_init_mode_masks(struct device *dev, unsigned int usid,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static bool mt6315_mode_mask_owned(struct device *dev, u32 rails, u32 phases)
+{
+	/* Preserve legacy coupled outputs unless the board declares its phases. */
+	if (!of_find_property(dev->of_node, "mediatek,buck1-mode-mask", NULL))
+		return true;
+
+	return !(rails & BIT(MT6315_VBUCK1)) || !(phases & ~rails);
+}
+
 static int mt6315_regulator_probe(struct spmi_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
@@ -303,6 +312,11 @@ static int mt6315_regulator_probe(struct spmi_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Invalid BUCK mode mask\n");
 
+	/* Explicit mode changes must not write phases outside this provider. */
+	if (!mt6315_mode_mask_owned(dev, mask,
+				    init_data->modeset_mask[MT6315_VBUCK1]))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "BUCK mode mask includes unowned rails\n");
+
 	chip->dev = dev;
 	chip->regmap = regmap;
 	dev_set_drvdata(dev, chip);
